> > add a '. So if the fu'ivla was {.enri}, the lujvo for milli- and
> micro-henry 
> > would be {mily'enri} and {miky'enri}.
> 
> And this doesn't break anything?

No, because y'V is not otherwise used for anything. The only thing
to keep in mind is that a fuhivla rafsi can only be preceded by
a y-rafsi, but this is not a big restriction because every gismu
has at least one y-rafsi. This applies to every fu'ivla rafsi, not 
just those that start with a vowel.

